    "explanation": "To both parties. The distance is not in dispute. Under POL-RD-01 the governing figure is the trace (EV-GPS-00111): 29.98 km against a booked optimal of 24.0 km on EV-TRIP-00111, an excess of 5.98 km or 24.9% — past both the 0.8 km and the 20% gate, so a deviation is established. The trip_record's rounded 30.0 km is not relied on, as POL-RD-01 forbids citing it for this test.\n\nThe deviation is excused under POL-RD-03. EV-ADVIS-00111-01 is a live LTA DataMall advisory (type CLOSURE, severity HIGH) for the Pan Island Expressway towards Tuas, after the Clementi Rd exit — the expressway the optimal route uses, as EV-TRIP-00111 records it (BKE southbound then PIE westbound) and as the rider's own claim describes it ('on the BKE and the PIE'). Its window, 07:10 to 09:30, brackets the whole trip (07:47:40 to 08:25:40). The clean 10-second trace (229 fixes, 100% coverage, no gaps, maximum gap 0 s) shows the vehicle leaving the corridor at Bukit Panjang before the closed segment, taking Upper Bukit Timah Road — the diversion the advisory itself names — and rejoining on the AYE after it. Limbs (a), (b) and (c) are met. The rider is right that the optimal route's own polyline is not stored, so the derived 'trace enters the advisory area' fact (12 fixes inside, minimum distance 0.0 m) decides nothing by itself and is not used alone; the advisory's named corridor, the trip record's routing source and the trace's leave-before/rejoin-after pattern carry the limbs together.\n\nThe exoneration cap does not bite: min(measured 5.98 km, 1.30 x (29.2 - 24.0) + 1.00) = min(5.98, 7.76) = 5.98 km, so the whole excess is excused and nothing falls through to a POL-RD-02 distance refund. Even on the branch the driver concedes, recomputing per POL-RD-02 against the closure-adjusted optimal (29.98 km; duration 30.0 x 29.98/24.0 = 37.5 min) gives (3.80 + 0.75 x 29.98 + 0.28 x 37.5) x 1.0, the surge multiplier read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, + 0.80 platform fee = 37.585 against charged_total 37.74 — a difference of 0.155, below the SGD 0.50 de minimis, so NO_ACTION in any event.\n\nThe rider's remaining claims do not change this. POL-RD-04 does not apply: the only instruction in the chat log (EV-CHAT-00111) is the driver's, and the rider's reply ('as long as i reach by 8.30') names no place or road and carries no waypoint_hint, so no distance is excluded as rider-requested — the point simply does not arise. POL-RD-09 has nothing to correct: tolls_erp and optimal_route_erp_sgd are 0.00, erp_gantries is empty and no surcharge line exists, so there is no pass-through to refund and no billing-integrity defect. POL-RD-06 is not engaged: the deviation is not MATERIAL (24.9% is under 50% and 5.98 km under 8.0 km) and the driver's trailing-90-day figures — deviation_flags_90d 0 against 588 completed trips — establish no pattern, so no uplift and no conduct referral. The alternative plea for escalation under POL-RD-10(5) is rejected: the driver cited an advisory that is present in the bundle, covers the trip window and names the corridor the optimal route uses, so nothing was invoked against a missing or inadequate artifact; and no other POL-RD-10 trigger fires (identifiers match across trip record, trace and fare breakdown; timestamps run forward and agree; the trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c); the figures are far below the refund ceiling; every charge line reconciles).\n\nResult: the excess was caused by a genuine, documented road closure that the driver correctly avoided, and the fare charged is within SGD 0.05 of the fare the closure-adjusted route warrants. The rider's claim is not supported and the present state stands on paid-for services. This differs from precedents P-0001 and P-0002, which ran on POL-RD-01, POL-RD-02 and POL-RD-08 and ended in partial refunds: neither of those had a live traffic advisory excusing the whole of the excess, which is what decides this case. The monetary effect is nil."
